      "title": "Mississippi University for Women",
      "description": "Mississippi University for Women | CPDC Speech Path Student Aide-Institutional Fall 2026 Skip to Main Content Home About The W ACADEMICS & MAJORS Admissions SUPPORT NEWS Directories . Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Employment Non-Faculty Employment Student Employment CPDC Speech Path Student Aide-Institutional Fall 2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Justification Position Information Position Title CPDC Speech Path Student Aide-Institutional Fall 2026 Unit Name Child and Parent Development Center Salary Grade Student (Institutional) Number of Months Student Worker Full-time or Part-time Part-Time Hours per week 15 Proposed Annual Salary, Hourly Rate or One-time payment Essential Duties Help keep the health and safety of the children first. Assist in the center complying with all requirements as per Mississippi Department of Health Child Care Regulations. Serve as a classroom teacher’s aide to assist with classroom cleanliness, meal times, hygiene needs, special projects, curriculum, center based play, and routines. Any other duties, as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Must be loving, patient, kind, and willing to take directions and work hard. Must have strong communication skills. Mississippi Immunization 121 form/record required. Prefer, but not required, for student to have recent First Aid/ CPR training. Prefer, but not required, for student to have current MS Letter of Suitability to work in childcare. A LOS is required with hire. Background checks and state health and safety training required when hired. Early childhood, education, family studies or any coursework related to child development is a plus. Email cpdc@muw.edu with questions. Job Description Summary MUW’s Child and Parent Development Center is a childcare center and preschool on the MUW campus. We provide high-quality early childhood learning experiences to MUW’s youngest learners and serve as the laboratory school for the Division of Education and Outreach. The primary job is to keep the safety and needs of the children first. Assist teachers with implementing classroom curriculum and activities in small and large groups and one-on-one. Comply with all regulations from the Mississippi Department of Health, and comply with all rules and regulations of MUW’s Child and Parent Development Center. Only Speech and Language Pathology Students can apply Hours of Availability CPDC is open with varying shifts available between 7:15-5:30. We are open year round and abide by the employee holiday schedule for closure. https://www.muw.edu/hr/employees/holidays Background Check Statement Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. However, failure to disclose may disqualify a candidate. Requisition Detail Information Open Date 04/15/2026 Will this job have a specific close date? No Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Student workers are required to be enrolled in at least 6 credit hours in the semester in which they work.\r\n\r\nRegistration in less than 6 hours at MUW makes you ineligible to be a student worker.\r\n\r\nAre you currently enrolled  or will you be enrolled in at least 6 credit hours at MUW in the semester for which you are applying for student employment? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work Study? (If you are unsure, or you have not yet been awarded Federal Work Study, please contact the Student Financial Aid office at (662)329-7114.) Yes No * Please provide your 9-digit MUW Student ID number: (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently majoring in Speech-Language Pathology? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume © 2013 Mississippi University for Women Columbus, MS 39701 / 662-329-7106 Non Discriminating Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
