    "https://muw.peopleadmin.com/postings/6515": {
      "title": "Mississippi University for Women",
      "description": "Mississippi University for Women | Intramural Official (multiple openings) Skip to Main Content Home About The W ACADEMICS & MAJORS Admissions SUPPORT NEWS Directories . Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Employment Non-Faculty Employment Student Employment Intramural Official (multiple openings) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please provide a brief writing sample explaining why you want to work for Intramural Sports. Position Justification Position Information Position Title Intramural Official (multiple openings) Unit Name Campus Recreation Salary Grade Student (Institutional) Number of Months Student Worker Full-time or Part-time Part-Time Hours per week 5-10 Proposed Annual Salary, Hourly Rate or One-time payment Essential Duties Fulfill schedule obligations Penalize, in accordance with the rules of the sport and the regulations of the department, any unsportsmanlike conduct by players Knowledge of the rules governing each sport and regulations of the department Positive attitude toward work and fellow officials Attempt to resolve problems if possible Receive and document protests, and then immediately contact the sport supervisor on duty Minimum Qualifications Must be available to work late afternoon and evenings Monday through Thursday. Job Description Summary Responsible for maintaining a safe and pleasant playing environment for all participants by enforcing the established rules and regulations for each particular sport. Hours of Availability Background Check Statement Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. However, failure to disclose may disqualify a candidate. Requisition Detail Information Open Date 05/27/2025 Will this job have a specific close date? No Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please provide a brief writing sample explaining why you want to work for Intramural Sports. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Student workers are required to be enrolled in at least 6 credit hours in the semester in which they work.\r\n\r\nRegistration in less than 6 hours at MUW makes you ineligible to be a student worker.\r\n\r\nAre you currently enrolled  or will you be enrolled in at least 6 credit hours at MUW in the semester for which you are applying for student employment? Yes No * Do you have any officiating experience? Yes No * List any sports that you have played. (Open Ended Question) * What sports would you be interested in officiating? Flag Football Softball Basketball All of the above Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Resume © 2013 Mississippi University for Women Columbus, MS 39701 / 662-329-7106 Non Discriminating Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
