pool. Lifeguards must have a current Lifeguard and CPR for the Professional Rescuer certification. Hours of Availability See required document Background Check Statement Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. However, failure to disclose may disqualify a candidate. Requisition Detail Information Requisition Number FY20691NF Open Date 09/29/2025 Will this job have a specific close date? No Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants 1. Please provide Hours of Availability in the application. 2. Attach Lifeguard Certification to “Other Document” portal. *Must be currently certified as a Lifeguard. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? MUW Departmental Announcement MUW Human Resources Office MUW Website Mississippi Employment Service Local Newspaper In-state Newspaper Out-of-state Newspaper The Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com Friend Journal/Periodical Off-campus Recruitment Women/Minority Publication Contacted by department and invited to apply Other The Academic Network (TAN) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States? (Proof of Citizenship or Immigration status will be required upon offer of employment) Yes No * If hired, would you need sponsorship or work authorization to work for MUW now or in the future?  (NOTE:  MUW does not sponsor employment visas.) Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Other Document Optional Documents © 2013 Mississippi University for Women Columbus, MS 39701 / 662-329-7106 Non Discriminating Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
