    "https://muw.peopleadmin.com/postings/6953": {
      "title": "Mississippi University for Women",
      "description": "Mississippi University for Women | Long Blue Line Auction Fundraising Intern Skip to Main Content Home About The W ACADEMICS & MAJORS Admissions SUPPORT NEWS Directories . Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Employment Non-Faculty Employment Student Employment Long Blue Line Auction Fundraising Intern Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please submit your resume and a cover letter explaining your interest in the Auction Fundraising Intern position and how your skills align with our organization's mission. Position Justification Position Information Position Title Long Blue Line Auction Fundraising Intern Unit Name Office of Development & Alumni Salary Grade Student (Institutional) Number of Months Student Worker Full-time or Part-time Part-Time Hours per week 10-15 Proposed Annual Salary, Hourly Rate or One-time payment Essential Duties Assist in the planning and organization of MUW Alumni Association ( MUWAA ) fundraising auctions, including acquiring auction items, coordinating logistics, and managing event materials. Conduct research to identify potential donors, sponsors, and auction items to enhance event offerings. Collaborate with the MUW Office of Development and Alumni team, and the MUWAA Special Events Committee to create promotional materials for auctions, including social media content, and email campaigns. Support the development of auction catalogs and item descriptions, ensuring accuracy and appeal to potential bidders. Assist during auction events by managing auction items, facilitating bidder inquiries, and supporting the MUW Special Events Committee as needed Aid in post-event activities, including donor acknowledgments, data entry, shipping items, and event evaluation. May include some auction wrap up responsibilities. Minimum Qualifications Pursuing a degree in Business, Marketing, Nonprofit Management, or related field. Strong organizational skills with the ability to multitask and prioritize effectively in a fast-paced environment. Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal. Detail-oriented with a keen eye for accuracy in donor communications and event materials. Maintain professionalism, adhering to MUW policies and ethical standard while upholding confidentiality to ensure the protection and security of sensitive donor information. Proficiency in Microsoft Office suite and familiarity with fundraising software, social media content creation, graphic design, or databases is a plus. Passion for our organization’s mission and a desire to contribute to fundraising efforts. Job Description Summary As an Auction Fundraising Intern, you will play a key role in supporting our fundraising efforts by assisting in the planning, coordination, and execution of auction events. This internship offers hands-on experience in event management, donor relations, and fundraising strategies within a dynamic and impactful organization. Hands-on experience in fundraising and event management within a nonprofit environment. Mentorship and guidance from experienced professionals in the field. Networking opportunities with donors, sponsors, and industry professionals. A chance to make a meaningful impact and contribute to a noble cause. Hours of Availability Background Check Statement Requisition Detail Information Open Date 06/12/2026 Will this job have a specific close date? No Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please submit your resume and a cover letter explaining your interest in the Auction Fundraising Intern position and how your skills align with our organization’s mission. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Student workers are required to be enrolled in at least 6 credit hours in the semester in which they work.\r\n\r\nRegistration in less than 6 hours at MUW makes you ineligible to be a student worker.\r\n\r\nAre you currently enrolled  or will you be enrolled in at least 6 credit hours at MUW in the semester for which you are applying for student employment? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents © 2013 Mississippi University for Women Columbus, MS 39701 / 662-329-7106 Non Discriminating Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
