      "title": "Mississippi University for Women",
      "description": "Mississippi University for Women | Oral History Intern Skip to Main Content Home About The W ACADEMICS & MAJORS Admissions SUPPORT NEWS Directories . Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Employment Non-Faculty Employment Student Employment Oral History Intern Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Justification Position Information Position Title Oral History Intern Unit Name Center for Women's Research & Public Policy Salary Grade Student (Institutional) Number of Months Student Worker Full-time or Part-time Part-Time Hours per week 10-20 Proposed Annual Salary, Hourly Rate or One-time payment Essential Duties After receiving training, transcribe recorded Golden Girls Oral History interviews, ensuring accuracy and completeness. Assist Center Director in organizing records, including audio files, related to the Golden Girls Oral History interviews and in depositing these in the university archives . Coordinate with the Center Director and the University Archivist to digitize Golden Girls Oral History Project interviews and related records and incorporate them into the Beulah Culbertson Archives and Special Collections at Fant Memorial Library. As needed, Assist Center Director in planning and implementing the upcoming Golden Girls Oral History interview, including participant recruitment and interview scheduling. Minimum Qualifications Proﬁciency with Microsoft Oﬃce products and ability to type accurately and efficiently. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, especially regarding listening and aural comprehension Attention to detail Ability to work independently and meet deadlines Interest in the history of Mississippi University for Women and women’s social history more generally Job Description Summary The MUW Center for Women’s Research & Public Policy ( CWRRP ) seeks a student intern to transcribe recorded interviews from the Golden Girls Oral History Project and to work with the CWRRP Director and university Archivist to organize and digitize interviews and records related to the project, incorporating them into the Culbertson Archives and making them accessible to the general public. Hours of Availability Flexible in coordination with the Center Director Background Check Statement Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. However, failure to disclose may disqualify a candidate. Requisition Detail Information Open Date 10/03/2025 Will this job have a specific close date? No Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Student workers are required to be enrolled in at least 6 credit hours in the semester in which they work.\r\n\r\nRegistration in less than 6 hours at MUW makes you ineligible to be a student worker.\r\n\r\nAre you currently enrolled  or will you be enrolled in at least 6 credit hours at MUW in the semester for which you are applying for student employment? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work Study? (If you are unsure, or you have not yet been awarded Federal Work Study, please contact the Student Financial Aid office at (662)329-7114.) Yes No * Please provide your 9-digit MUW Student ID number: (Open Ended Question) 