    "https://muw.peopleadmin.com/postings/6844": {
      "title": "Mississippi University for Women",
      "description": "Mississippi University for Women | Admissions Ambassador Skip to Main Content Home About The W ACADEMICS & MAJORS Admissions SUPPORT NEWS Directories . Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Employment Non-Faculty Employment Student Employment Admissions Ambassador Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Justification Position Information Position Title Admissions Ambassador Unit Name Admissions Salary Grade Student (Institutional) Number of Months Student Worker Full-time or Part-time Part-Time Hours per week Less than 20 hours per week. Proposed Annual Salary, Hourly Rate or One-time payment Essential Duties Meet with prospective students and their families and cover student life, academic options, and the application process. Aid in Telecounseling. Assisting the Admissions Office with daily office duties, recruitment events, conducting tours, meeting with prospective students and parents, and other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications All members must maintain a minimum of 12 hours per semester and a 2.5 or better grade point average. All members must work a minimum of 10 hours per week. All members must conduct a required number of campus tours. Ambassadors may be asked to participate in activities that occur, not only during the day, but possibly at night or during the weekend. All members will attend college days and/or nights at an assigned school. They will also make recruiting visits with MUW Admissions Counselors during the year. In order to be eligible to apply for a Student Ambassador position, a student must have at least a 2.5 cumulative G.P.A. and have been a student at MUW for an entire academic year. Job Description Summary The W Ambassadors support the recruitment of potential students as an extension of the Office of Admissions. An Ambassador must represent the best of what The W Student Body has to offer. Our Admissions Student Ambassadors meet with prospective students and their families as part of their campus visit experience. They cover a broad range of topics, including student life, academic options, and the application process. Our Student Ambassadors are trained by our Admissions Counselors, and many are active in leadership positions across campus. Ambassadors will also aid in our Telecounseling efforts. Telecounseling is a recruitment strategy aimed at building relationships with prospective students over the telephone. It consists of frequent, ongoing telephone contact at critical points in each person’s decision-making process. Hours of Availability Background Check Statement Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. However, failure to disclose may disqualify a candidate. Requisition Detail Information Open Date 03/05/2026 Will this job have a specific close date? No Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Student workers are required to be enrolled in at least 6 credit hours in the semester in which they work.\r\n\r\nRegistration in less than 6 hours at MUW makes you ineligible to be a student worker.\r\n\r\nAre you currently enrolled  or will you be enrolled in at least 6 credit hours at MUW in the semester for which you are applying for student employment? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents © 2013 Mississippi University for Women Columbus, MS 39701 / 662-329-7106 Non Discriminating Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://muw.peopleadmin.com/postings/7040": {
      "title": "Position Justification",
      "description": "Mississippi University for Women | Foundation Accountant Skip to Main Content Home About The W ACADEMICS & MAJORS Admissions SUPPORT NEWS Directories . Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Employment Non-Faculty Employment Student Employment Foundation Accountant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In \"Other Document\" please upload additional information about your experience: Using Excel for financial reporting and if you have advanced experience, such as pivot tables and macros. Your familiarity with software and tools commonly used in non-profit accounting, whether you have experience in Blackbaud Financial Edge and if so, describe your experience with the software. Managing budgets and financial forecasts. Position Justification Position Information Click here to view Salary Grade Position Title Foundation Accountant Unit Name Office of Development & Alumni Salary Grade 8 Number of Months 12 months Full-time or Part-time Full-Time Hours per week 40 Proposed Annual Salary, Hourly Rate or One-time payment Essential Duties Responsible for day-to-day accounting functions ensuring accuracy and completeness of financial records and reports. Reconciliation of cash, checks, merchant accounts, PayPal and Venmo and maintaining proper cash balances. Reconciliation of investments, allocations, management fees and due to/due from entries. Preparation of all monthly financial reports required by Foundation board and the University. Preparation of reports for quarterly restricted funds, grant reports and special funds reports. Prepare and post monthly journal entries, adjusting journal entries and re-classifications. Reconciliation of credit card statements and processing of accounts payable. Process all invoices for payment to vendors and reimbursements. In partnership with the Executive Director, prepare an annual budget of the Foundation for review and approval by the Foundation board. Assist in preparing investment committee and finance committee items for meetings and board agenda. Prepare audit working papers and reports needed by independent auditors to complete annual audit and tax returns. Prepare documents needed for independent firm to ensure timely filing of charitable registrations as required by various states. Oversee University budget for the Office of Development & Alumni. Maintain schedules and timelines, organize multiple projects efficiently and effectively. Calculate annual endowment awards for scholarships and other funds. Provide scholarship award amounts to Financial Aid and work to ensure prospering awarding of funds. Maintain current scholarship criteria and provide to Financial Aid. Reconcile university invoices for scholarships and program awards. Preparation of endowment annual reports to donors. Participation in the Office of Development & Alumni events and oversee event financial management. Participate in Foundation board meetings, investment and finance committee meetings. Supervise Accounting Assistant/ Office Supervisor. Performs other reasonable duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree in accounting, finance, or a related field; MBA or CPA preferred At least seven years of progressively responsible experience in financial management, with a working knowledge of the nonprofit sector Skills and Abilities: Preferred in-depth understanding of generally accepted accounting principles ( GAAP ) with additional understanding and experience specific to Not-For-Profit Financial Reporting standards under Financial Accounting Standards Board ( FASB ) Proven track record of successful financial management, including experience developing and implementing financial strategies, managing budgets/investments, and overseeing financial reporting and compliance Strong leadership and management skills; interest in working as a member of a team Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to communicate financial information to non-financial stakeholders Knowledge of MUW ; alumnus preferred Ability to work with intricate computer systems, including Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge, Financial Edge, Award Management and Microsoft Office suite. Expertise in Excel to include pivot tables and advanced formulas required Ability to handle multiple projects simultaneously. Ability to accomplish stated goals Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to talk or hear, regularly required to stand; walk and sit and occasionally use hands to finger, handle, or feel; reach with hands and arms; climb or balance and stoop kneel, crouch, or crawl. The employee is regularly required to lift and/or move up to 25 pounds. Vision requirements include close, distance and peripheral vision and ability to adjust focus. Job Description Summary The Foundation Accountant (FA) will be responsible for the day-to-day financial operation of the MUW Foundation (Foundation), ensuring our organization’s financial health, growth, and sustainability. The FA will manage the Foundation’s financial reporting, assist with annual budgeting, financial analysis, investment strategy and annual audit. The FA will work closely with the Executive Director and Board of Directors to develop and implement financial strategies that support our organization’s mission, vision and goals. Hours of Availability Background Check Statement Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. However, failure to disclose may disqualify a candidate. Requisition Detail Information Requisition Number FY20781NF Open Date 09/08/2026 Will this job have a specific close date? No Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants In “Other Document” please upload additional information about your experience: Using Excel for financial reporting and if you have advanced experience, such as pivot tables and macros. Your familiarity with software and tools commonly used in non-profit accounting, whether you have experience in Blackbaud Financial Edge and if so, describe your experience with the software. Managing budgets and financial forecasts. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? MUW Departmental Announcement MUW Human Resources Office MUW Website Mississippi Employment Service Local Newspaper In-state Newspaper Out-of-state Newspaper The Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com Friend Journal/Periodical Off-campus Recruitment Women/Minority Publication Contacted by department and invited to apply Other The Academic Network (TAN) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States? (Proof of Citizenship or Immigration status will be required upon offer of employment) Yes No * If hired, would you need sponsorship or work authorization to work for MUW now or in the future?  (NOTE:  MUW does not sponsor employment visas.) Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Optional Documents © 2013 Mississippi University for Women Columbus, MS 39701 / 662-329-7106 Non Discriminating Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://muw.peopleadmin.com/postings/7043": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Chemistry",
      "description": "Mississippi University for Women | Assistant or Associate Professor of Chemistry Skip to Main Content Home About The W ACADEMICS & MAJORS Admissions SUPPORT NEWS Directories . Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Employment Non-Faculty Employment Student Employment Assistant or Associate Professor of Chemistry Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Being authorized to work in the United States is a precondition of employment, and MUW does not sponsor work visas. To be eligible for this position, you will need to be authorized to work in the U.S. on a full-time basis now and in the future. MUW does not hire individuals who require employer sponsored visas. Consideration of complete applications will begin Nov 1, 2026, and continue until a successful candidate is hired. For more information about the position, contact Dr. Xiaoxia Li (662) 329-8561 or email xli@muw.edu. Visit the link https://muw.peopleadmin.com to upload required documents for application. Please provide: CV Cover letter Statement of teaching philosophy (no more than 2 pages) Plan for undergraduate-centered research in Organic Chemistry (no more than 2 pages) Information for three contacts that can provide reference letters Documents should be uploaded in the \"Applicant Documents Section” under “Other Documents”. Position Justification Position Information Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Chemistry Unit Name Sciences and Mathematics Salary Grade Faculty Number of Months 9 months Full-time or Part-time Full-Time Hours per week 40 Annual Salary or Hourly Rate Range Essential Duties The successful candidate will teach Organic Chemistry , General Chemistry, instrumental courses and courses in their area of expertise. Service to the department, university, and community is expected along with a commitment to the scholarship of teaching and learning at a diverse, primarily undergraduate institution. Applications should also have a viable research plan that incorporates undergraduate involvement. Additional start-up funding from NIH’s MS- INBRE (IDeA Network of Biomedical Research Excellence) might be available if the research area relates to biomedical or public health fields. Applicants may be considered that are near the completion of their doctoral degree, but completion of their degree within a year (August 2028) will be required for their continued employment. In addition to campus resources, Interactions and collaborations are also possible with Mississippi State University, a Research-I institution that is a 25-minute drive from campus. Minimum Qualifications It is preferred that applicants have a doctorate in organic chemistry, or a related chemistry field, and a commitment to the scholarship of teaching and learning. Job Description Summary Applications are invited for a tenure-track position in ORGANIC CHEMISTRY at either Assistant Professor or Associate Professor level, commensurate with experience, beginning August 2027. To enter at the Associate Professor level, candidates must have several years of undergraduate teaching experience and a track record of involving undergraduates in research projects. The successful candidate will teach Organic Chemistry , General Chemistry, instrumental courses, and courses in their area of expertise. Salary information for this position can be found on the application page https://muw.peopleadmin.com . Service to the department, university, and community is expected along with a commitment to the scholarship of teaching and learning at a diverse, primarily undergraduate institution. Applications should also have a viable research plan that incorporates undergraduate involvement. Additional start-up funding from NIH’s MS- INBRE (IDeA Network of Biomedical Research Excellence) might be available if the research area relates to biomedical or public health fields. Applicants may be considered that are near the completion of their doctoral degree, but completion of their degree within a year (August 2028) will be required for their continued employment. In addition to campus resources, Interactions and collaborations are also possible with Mississippi State University, a Research-I institution that is a 25-minute drive from campus. Mississippi University for Women ( MUW ) is a public coeducational, primarily undergraduate, liberal arts institution serving an economically and racially diverse student body with a total annual enrollment of over 2200 students. The University emphasizes a student-centered learning environment that includes research opportunities. Additional information can be found on the MUW website: http://www.muw.edu . All hires contingent upon successful completion of a background check. Mississippi University for Women is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Background Check Statement Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. However, failure to disclose may disqualify a candidate. Requisition Detail Information Requisition Number FY20285F Open Date 09/10/2026 Will this job have a specific close date? No Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Being authorized to work in the United States is a precondition of employment, and MUW does not sponsor work visas. To be eligible for this position, you will need to be authorized to work in the U.S. on a full-time basis now and in the future. MUW does not hire individuals who require employer sponsored visas. Consideration of complete applications will begin Nov 1, 2026, and continue until a successful candidate is hired. For more information about the position, contact Dr. Xiaoxia Li (662) 329-8561 or email xli@muw.edu. Visit the link https://muw.peopleadmin.com to upload required documents for application. Please provide: CV Cover letter Statement of teaching philosophy (no more than 2 pages) Plan for undergraduate-centered research in Organic Chemistry (no more than 2 pages) Information for three contacts that can provide reference letters Documents should be uploaded in the \"Applicant Documents Section” under “Other Documents”. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? MUW Departmental Announcement MUW Human Resources Office MUW Website Mississippi Employment Service Local Newspaper In-state Newspaper Out-of-state Newspaper The Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs.com Friend Journal/Periodical Off-campus Recruitment Women/Minority Publication Contacted by department and invited to apply Other The Academic Network (TAN) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States? (Proof of Citizenship or Immigration status will be required upon offer of employment) Yes No * If hired, would you need sponsorship or work authorization to work for MUW now or in the future?  (NOTE:  MUW does not sponsor employment visas.) Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcript 1 Other Document Optional Documents Unofficial Transcript 2 Unofficial Transcript 3 © 2013 Mississippi University for Women Columbus, MS 39701 / 662-329-7106 Non Discriminating Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
