      "description": "Mississippi University for Women | Student Worker-Information Systems-Lab monitor Skip to Main Content Home About The W ACADEMICS & MAJORS Admissions SUPPORT NEWS Directories . Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Employment Non-Faculty Employment Student Employment Student Worker-Information Systems-Lab monitor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Justification Position Information Position Title Student Worker-Information Systems-Lab monitor Unit Name N/A Salary Grade Student (Institutional) Number of Months Student Worker Full-time or Part-time N/A Hours per week 10 Proposed Annual Salary, Hourly Rate or One-time payment Essential Duties Ensure the security of the building and property in the building while assisting current faculty, staff, and students of MUW . Minimum Qualifications Enrolled for at least 6 credit hours. Job Description Summary Ensure the security of the building and property in the building while assisting current faculty, staff, and students of MUW Hours of Availability 7:30am – 7:00pm Background Check Statement Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. However, failure to disclose may disqualify a candidate. Requisition Detail Information Open Date 09/14/2026 Will this job have a specific close date? No Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Student workers are required to be enrolled in at least 6 credit hours in the semester in which they work.\r\n\r\nRegistration in less than 6 hours at MUW makes you ineligible to be a student worker.\r\n\r\nAre you currently enrolled  or will you be enrolled in at least 6 credit hours at MUW in the semester for which you are applying for student employment? Yes No * Have you been awarded Federal Work Study? (If you are unsure, or you have not yet been awarded Federal Work Study, please contact the Student Financial Aid office at (662)329-7114.) Yes No * Please provide your 9-digit MUW Student ID number: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents © 2013 Mississippi University for Women Columbus, MS 39701 / 662-329-7106 Non Discriminating Policy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
